"""
Choice between two signals fixed by a structural parameter: y = u1 when `on`, else y = u2.

Ports: `u1` the signal passed when `on`, `u2` the signal passed otherwise, `y` the selected
signal.

The choice is made when the model is compiled, so the unselected input drops out of the
equations and the switch causes no events. Both inputs always exist and must both be wired: to
gate a signal off, feed `u2` its fallback value from a constant. For a choice that changes during
a run, use `BlockComponents.Logical.Switch`.
"""
component ParameterSwitch
  extends BlockComponents.Interfaces.SI2SO
  "Pass u1 rather than u2"
  structural parameter on::Boolean = true
relations
  if on
    y = u1
  else
    y = u2
  end
end
